Modifications made in this project include, without limitation:
  * replacement of the Tauri desktop shell with a Node.js/Express server
  * multi-user accounts, email/password sign-in, and TOTP second factors
  * server-side per-user library storage (playlists and liked songs)
  * song recommendations between registered accounts, with Web Push delivery
    and a documented bearer-key-compatible HTTP API
  * twelve built-in interface themes plus custom CSS theme support, with an
    admin-set instance default that also styles the sign-in page
  * Discord Rich Presence driven from the server, with per-account settings,
    a custom status message, and per-account "Secret Show" exceptions that
    keep chosen songs off the profile
  * an offline feature that stores audio in the listener's own browser
    storage (IndexedDB) rather than on a shared server disk; the server
    relays audio for playback without writing audio files to its own disk
  * a shared server-side artwork and API-response cache
  * Docker packaging and self-hosted API documentation
  * removal of the Last.fm integration

